# Infrastructure safety

## Environment distinction

| Env | Agent posture |
|-----|----------------|
| Local / this git repo | Safe for versionable kit/docs changes |
| Staging | Measure first; no invent of host layout |
| Production (`nortiqalab.com` / VPS SC2027) | Read-only public checks unless Gio + gates |

Never assume a path, container name, or Compose project belongs to Nortiqa without evidence.

## Forbidden by default

- Delete images, networks, volumes, or containers
- `docker system prune` or mass cleanup
- Remote host edits, Nginx reload, DNS changes
- Real migrations, data writes, secret changes
- Activating production n8n workflows automatically

## Docker / Compose (when present in a Nortiqa repo)

- Review Compose before `up`
- Avoid port conflicts; prefer documented ports
- Preserve backups; do not wipe volumes
- This org-profile repo currently has **no** Docker/Compose files

## External dependencies (known public map)

- Site / API / n8n / MCP hostnames in `agents/BOOTSTRAP.md`
- Prefer staging checks before any prod change proposal
- Ollama remains private on loopback

## n8n / webhooks (product work guidance)

When implementing webhooks elsewhere in Nortiqa:

- Separate Test URL vs Production URL
- Prefer versioned routes when fitting (`POST /api/v1/<service>` as a pattern, not a mandate)
- Validate payloads; authenticate; consider idempotency
- Explicit HTTP responses; distinguish Webhook vs Respond to Webhook nodes
- No secrets in URLs; log errors without leaking credentials
- Document request/response contracts
- Do not auto-activate production workflows from agent sessions
